        "original_id": "3141f90d-0533-5903-a13c-f6f5c7d483f6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Equestria\n- Organizations/Nations: The Kingdom of Equestria\n- Products: Hasbro's animated show, its feature film\n- Peoples/Groups: unicorns, pegasi, earth ponies\n- Characters/Creatures: Wendigos, Ithaqua\n- People: H. P. Lovecraft\n- Concepts: Wendigo psychosis, Cthulhu Mythos\n\nFacts:\n- The Kingdom of Equestria, or simply Equestria, is the primary setting for Hasbro's animated show and its feature film.\n- The nation of Equestria was founded when the three pony tribes—unicorns, pegasi, and earth ponies—came together in harmony to fight the Wendigos and stop an eternal blizzard.\n- Wendigo psychosis is a controversial modern medical term described by psychiatrists as a culture-bound syndrome involving an intense craving for human flesh and a fear of becoming a cannibal.\n- Ithaqua, also called the \"Wind-Walker\" or the \"Wendigo,\" is a fictional character in H. P. Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "84caba6e-85f7-5386-9e59-161477bc650b",
        "text": "Page: Equestria. Sentence: The Kingdom of Equestria, or simply, Equestria, is the primary setting for Hasbro's animated show, \"\", and its feature film \"\".\nPage: Equestria. Sentence: The nation was founded when the three pony tribes, unicorns, pegasi, and earth ponies, came together to in harmony, to fight the Wendigos, and to stop an eternal blizzard.\nPage: Wendigo. Sentence: The legend lends its name to the controversial modern medical term Wendigo psychosis, described by psychiatrists as a culture-bound syndrome with symptoms such as an intense craving for human flesh and a fear of becoming a cannibal.\nPage: Ithaqua. Sentence: Ithaqua (the \"Wind-Walker\" or the \"Wendigo\") is a fictional character in the Cthulhu Mythos of H. P. Lovecraft.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
